nsistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.23262301736175406,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.08213941377779,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":66.1,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06789526079912686,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":86.6,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.010796065572962421,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":63.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00858172116089025,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":85.7,"_gate_insider_own":3.0000001e-05,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Nomura Holdings, Inc. engages in the provision of investment, financing, and related services to individual, institutional, and government clients worldwide. It operates through three segments: Wealth Management, Investment Management, and Wholesale. The Wealth Management segment offers asset management services. The Investment Management segment provides investment management services and investment solutions, such as establishing and managing investment trusts, discretionary investment services, investment and management for investment vehicles, funds for institutional investors, and management of silent partnerships. The Wholesale segment is involved in the sales and trading of debt and equity securities, foreign exchange; offers investment banking services, including underwriting and distribution of debt and equity securities, mergers and acquisitions, and financial advisory services. Nomura Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 1925 and is headquartered in Tokyo, Japan.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kentaro  Okuda | President, Group CEO, Representative Executive Officer & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $10.4M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 28K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Nomura Holdings Inc is a large-cap financial services business with a $27.5B market cap on $31.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 10% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The company is burning through $8.0B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"News sentiment sharply negative (-0.20) across 12 recent articles \u2014 the narrative has turned","sev":"red","cat":"news"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.1437478768363226},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 36% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Nomura Holdings reports 1H results (NYSE:NMR)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668194-nomura-holdings-reports-1h-results","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793977854.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(NMR) Volatility Zones as Tactical Triggers","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/16/NMR_Volatility_Zones_as_Tactical_Triggers_110626062602_1793964362.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793964362.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Post-waterfall recovery needs 1-